
## 1. What is Business (Business kya hai)

*Business ek **organized aur continuous economic activity** hai jis mein cheezein ya services **banai ya bechi** jati hain, **munafa** kamane ke liye aur logon ki **needs aur wants** poori karne ke liye. Isko **teen nazariyon** se dekhte hain: **General meaning** (kya karta hai), **Organizational view** (log milkar common maqsad ke liye kaam karte hain) aur **Economic perspective** (munasib qeemat ke badle organized exchange). **Griffin and Ebert (1996)** ki definition aur **comprehensive definition** dono exam mein likhni hain.*

---

## 2. Characteristics of Business (12 points)

*Mere dost ki dukaan ek **economic activity** hai jahan wo cheezein **banata ya bechta** hai, aur ye **munafa** ke liye hai. Ye kaam **regular aur lagatar** chalta hai, lekin **risk aur uncertainty** hamesha saath rehti hai. Wo cheez **qeemat ke badle** deta hai aur **customer ko khush** rakhta hai. Sab kuch **organized aur systematic** hota hai, **muashre ki zimmedari** nibhai jati hai, aur wo **qanoon aur akhlaq** ke andar rehta hai. Wo **resources aur technology** ka istemal karta hai, kyunke business ka mahol **dynamic aur competitive** hai.*

---

## 3. Objectives of Business (12 points)

*Business pehle **munafa kamana** chahta hai, phir **zinda aur mustahkam** rehna chahta hai, aur **barhna aur phailna** chahta hai. Wo **customer ko khush** rakhta hai aur **naye idea (innovation)** laata hai. Wo **rozgar paida** karta hai, **wasail ka behtareen istemal** karta hai, **malikon ko munasib return** deta hai aur **mulazimeen ki bhalai** ka khayal rakhta hai. Wo **muashre ki zimmedari** nibhata hai, **market ka leader** banna chahta hai, aur ye sab **qanoon aur akhlaq** ke andar rehkar karta hai.*

---

## 4. Role of Business in Economic Progress (15 points)

*Business **cheezein aur services paida** karta hai, **rozgar** deta hai, **qaumi aamdani (GDP)** barhata hai aur **munafa dobara lagakar sarmaya (capital formation)** banata hai. Wo **andruni tijarat** ko mazboot aur **bairooni tijarat** (export aur foreign exchange) ko wasee karta hai. **Technology** ko taraqqi deta hai, **sarkar ko tax** deta hai aur **infrastructure** banane mein madad karta hai. **Chhote karobar (SMEs)** ko sahara deta hai, **pichhre ilaqon** ko aage barhata hai aur **zindagi ka maiyaar** behtar karta hai. Naye **entrepreneurs** ko hausla deta hai, **samaji khidmat (CSR)** karta hai, aur mulk ko **maeeshi istehkam** deta hai.*

---

## 5. Initial Ethical Issues (10 points)

*Ek naya firm pehle apne **mulazimeen se insaaf** karta hai aur **imaandari aur shaffafiyat** se kaam leta hai. Wo apne **contracts mein integrity** rakhta hai, **customer ki zimmedari** nibhata hai aur **mahol ki hifazat** karta hai. Wo **data ki raaz-daari** rakhta hai, **mufaad ke takrao** se bachta hai, **sacha marketing** karta hai, **rishwat** se door rehta hai, aur **sab stakeholders ko sachchi tasveer** dikhata hai.*

---

## 6. Initial Legal Issues (10 points)

*Naya firm pehle **register** hota hai (business formation), phir apni **ijadaat mehfooz** karta hai (intellectual property) aur **contracts** likhta hai. Wo **mulazimeen ke qawaneen** aur **customer ke haqooq** ka khayal rakhta hai. Wo **sarkari qawaneen (regulatory compliance)** aur **tax** ki pairwi karta hai, **mahol** aur **data** ko mehfooz rakhta hai, aur **rishwat** se door rehta hai.*

**(Is ki tarteeb book ke mutabiq ye hai: Formation, IP, Employment, Regulatory, Taxation, Contract, Consumer, Environmental, Data, Anti-Bribery. Upar wali kahani tarteeb ko thora badal kar likhi gayi hai, is liye aap is tarteeb ko bhi ek baar dekh lein.)**

---

## 7. Business Permits and Licenses

**General categories (10):**
*Naya business pehle **General Business License** aur **Registration Certificate** leta hai, phir **Tax Registration** karwata hai aur agar zaroori ho to **Sales Tax/VAT Permit** leta hai. Mulazimeen rakhne par **Employer ID aur Labor Registration** karta hai. Jagah ke liye **Zoning permit**, sehat ke liye **Health and Safety permit**, aur mahol ke liye **Environmental permit** leta hai. Apne sector ke liye **Industry-Specific license** leta hai, aur aakhir mein apni cheezein **IP Registration** se mehfooz karta hai.*

**Pakistan ke 5 groups:**
*Pakistan mein startup pehle **Foundational Registrations** (SECP, NTN, Sales Tax) karwata hai, phir **Local Government Permits** (trade license, signboard, zoning) leta hai. Phir apne sector ke **Sector-Specific Licenses** (food, healthcare, education, IT), aur **Environmental aur Safety Permits** (EPA, fire safety). Aakhir mein **Other Regulatory Requirements** (import/export, IPO-Pakistan, EOBI, SBP/NEPRA/PEMRA) poori karta hai.*

---

## 8. Sole Proprietorship

**Features (10):**
*Is mein **ek hi malik** hota hai aur us ki **liability unlimited** hoti hai. **Shuru aur band karna aasan** hai, malik ke paas **poora control** hota hai lekin **sarmaya kam** hota hai. **Poora profit** malik ka hota hai, magar malik ke baghair **continuity nahi** rehti. Zimmedari **seedhi** malik ki hoti hai, **qanooni zaroorat kam** hain aur **maloomat private** rehti hain.*

**Advantages (9):**
*Ye **shuru karna aasan** hai, malik ka **poora control** hota hai aur **saara profit** us ka hota hai. **Qanooni jhanjhat kam** hain, malik ki **direct motivation** hoti hai aur **flexibility** milti hai. **Privacy** rehti hai, **kharcha kam** hota hai aur **customers se qareebi taluq** banta hai.*

**Disadvantages (7):**
*Malik ki **unlimited personal liability** hoti hai, **sarmaya kam**, **skills aur expertise limited**, aur **kaam ka bojh bohat zyada**. Malik ke baad **continuity khatam**, **expansion mushkil**, aur **faisle sirf ek insan ki nazar** se hote hain.*

---

## 9. Partnership

**Features (10):**
*Partners ek **voluntary agreement** karte hain, **tadad 2 se 20** hoti hai aur **profit-loss baanta** jata hai. Har partner **mutual agency** ke tahat firm ka agent hai, **liability unlimited** hai aur **assets ki co-ownership** hoti hai. Firm ki **zindagi limited** hai, ye **Partnership Act 1932** ke tahat chalti hai, har partner **capital lagata** hai, aur firm **alag legal entity nahi** hoti.*

**Advantages (10):**
*Partnership **banana aasan** hai, **resources mil jate** hain aur **zimmedari baant** jati hai. **Flexibility** milti hai, partners ki **skills ek dusre ka sahara** banti hain aur **profit sharing** hoti hai. **Capital tak rasai** behtar hoti hai, ek partner na ho to **decision-making chalti** rehti hai, **privacy** rehti hai aur **motivation aur commitment** barhte hain.*

**Disadvantages (9):**
*Partners ki **liability unlimited**, **jhagron ka khatra**, **zindagi limited** hoti hai. **Profit baantna** parta hai, **public ka aitmaad kam**, **bara sarmaya jama karna mushkil**. **Mutual agency ka risk** hota hai, **management efficiency limited**, aur firm ki **alag legal identity nahi**.*

---

## 10. Joint Stock Company

**Features (10):**
*Company **alag legal entity** hai, **limited liability** hai aur **perpetual succession** rakhti hai. Is ka **sarmaya shares** mein baanta hota hai jo **aasani se transfer** hote hain. Company ki **common seal** hoti hai, **Board of Directors** isay chalata hai, ye ek **artificial person** hai, **bara sarmaya** jama kar sakti hai aur **qanoon ke tahat** chalti hai.*

**Advantages (9):**
*Company mein **limited liability** aur **alag wujood** hai, **zindagi lambi** hai aur **bara sarmaya** mil sakta hai. **Shares aasani se transfer** hote hain, **professional management** hoti hai aur **economies of scale** milte hain. Company ki **credibility** hoti hai aur wo **lambay contracts** kar sakti hai.*

**Disadvantages (9):**
*Company ka **formation complex** aur **mehnga** hai, shareholders ka **managerial control kam** hai, **qanooni compliance sakht** hai aur **double taxation** hoti hai. **Secrecy nahi** rehti, **faislon mein deri** hoti hai, **ownership aur management alag** hote hain aur **profit baantna** parta hai.*

---

## 11. Mutual Agency aur Separate Legal Entity (aap ki list ke important concepts)

**Mutual Agency:**
*Partnership mein **har partner firm ka agent bhi hai aur principal bhi**. Agar ek partner **firm ke business ke daayre mein** koi sauda kar le, to **sab partners us se bandh** jate hain. Is ka **faida** tez faisle hai, lekin **nuqsan** ye ke ek ki ghalti sab ko le doobti hai.*

**Separate Legal Entity:**
*Registration ke baad **company apne shareholders se alag shakhs** ban jati hai. Wo **apne naam par jaidad** rakhti hai, **contracts** karti hai aur **muqadma** kar sakti hai. Isi liye shareholders ki **liability limited** aur company ki **zindagi perpetual** hoti hai.*

---

## 12. Business Registration Process in Pakistan

*Registration se karobar ko **legal recognition** milta hai, **limited liability ka tahaffuz**, **finance tak rasai**, **brand ki hifazat** aur **tax laws ki pairwi** hoti hai. Registration ke liye **5 structures** hain: **Sole Proprietorship, Partnership, Private Limited, Public Limited aur Single Member Company**. Sole aur partnership **FBR aur provincial authorities** ke paas, company **SECP** ke paas register hoti hai. **7 steps** hain: **structure chunna, naam chunna, digital signatures aur ID, SECP registration, NTN, sales tax aur licenses/permits**. Phir **documents** jama hote hain, aur registration ke baad **accounts, annual returns aur renewals** ka silsila chalta hai.*

---

## 13. Formation of Partnership Firm

*Partnership banane ke liye pehle **partners chune** jate hain, phir **Partnership Agreement** likha jata hai. Har partner ka **capital contribution** tay hota hai, firm ka **naam** chuna jata hai, aur **profit-loss ka ratio** tay hota hai. **Roles aur zimmedariyan** baanti jati hain, firm ka **registration** hota hai, **bank account** khola jata hai, **licenses aur permits** liye jate hain, aur aakhir mein **books of accounts** rakhe jate hain. Ye sab **Partnership Deed** mein likha hota hai aur **legal effects** ye hain ke partners **joint aur several zimmedar** hote hain.*

---

## 14. Formation of Company

*Company **teen stages** mein banti hai: pehle **Promotion**, jis mein **idea sochte, feasibility dekhte, sarmaya jama karte aur shuruati documents tayyar** karte hain. Phir **Incorporation**, jis mein **Memorandum aur Articles of Association** tayyar kar ke **Registrar** ko diye jate hain aur **Certificate of Incorporation** milta hai. Aakhir mein **Commencement of Business**: **private company** foran shuru kar sakti hai, jab ke **public company** ko pehle **prospectus** jari kar ke **minimum subscription** lena aur **Certificate of Commencement** hasil karna parta hai. Is ka **capital Authorized, Issued aur Paid-up** hissa mein hota hai aur registration ke baad company ko **alag legal status** milta hai.*

---

## Tips

- **Pehle kahani parhein, phir bina dekhe bolein.** Jahan atak jayein, wahi aap ki kamzori hai.
- **Tarteeb ka tareeqa:** har paragraph mein bold lafzon ko ek line ki tarah dohrayein.
- **Legal issues ki tarteeb:** upar noted kiya hai, is ko book se ek baar dekh lein.
- Is ke baad **chhota quiz** karna ho to bata dein, main Chapter 1 ke saare topics par bana deta hoon.
